+  // [ng2 ps5 port] Locks the mutex, spinning briefly first. The PS5's
+  // recursive mutex never spins: a thread that finds it taken goes straight
+  // to sleep in the kernel, and the holder makes a second system call on
+  // unlock to wake it. Nearly every hold of this lock is a few microseconds
+  // (a handle lookup, an event, page flags), so in heavy scenes the GPU
+  // command thread spent up to a fifth of its time in those sleeps and
